Uncaught overflow on clampToAssetsTotalScale. Wrap in try/catch for std::overflow_error like VaultDeposit/VaultClawback:

```suggestion:-0+10
    if (fix340Enabled && !isFinalWithdrawal && assetsWithdrawn > beast::kZero)
    {
        try
        {
            // Round Upward on the negative delta: the stored total is decremented by no more than it
            // can represent, so the payout is trimmed downward and the vault never pays out more than
            // it can account for.
            assetsWithdrawn =
                clampToAssetsTotalScale(vault, -assetsWithdrawn, Number::RoundingMode::Upward);
            // Payout collapsed to zero. Return tecPRECISION_LOSS instead of burning

Clamp can amplify delta when sfAssetsTotal mid-grid. Bound result to requested amount:

```suggestion
            if (assetsDeposited > amount)
                assetsDeposited = amount;
```

Moving `mptV2Enabled` outside is easier to read and cleaner
```
if (mptV2Enabled)
{
    if (trustlinesChanged_ != 0 && mptokensChanged_ != 0)
    ...
    if (tokenBefore_ && tokenAfter_ && tokenBefore_->getType() != tokenAfter_->getType())
    ...
}
```

If mptV2Enabled check is in the inner `if`, even when featureMPTokensV2 not enabled, the code check has no effect but will create some logs.

nit - alternatively could be (same for places down below)

```
if (!BEAST_EXPECT(vaultSle))
    return;
```

Non-fatal `BEAST_EXPECT` lets execution fall through to a null dereference on the next line. Use a guard:

```suggestion:-0+1
            if (!BEAST_EXPECT(vaultSle != nullptr))
                return;
```
